      "name": "AQL Search",
      "description": {
        "content": "Execute AQL queries to search for artifacts, builds, and entries",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "fc3b9ccc-2425-4031-90dd-502aace97704",
          "name": "JFrog Artifactory Execute AQL Query",
          "request": {
            "name": "JFrog Artifactory Execute AQL Query",
            "description": {
              "content": "Executes an Artifactory Query Language (AQL) query and returns matching results. AQL supports querying across multiple domains including items (artifacts), builds, entries, and more. Queries can include filtering, sorting, pagination, and inclusion of related entities.\n\nAQL query syntax follows the pattern:\n`domain.find(criteria).include(fields).sort(sort_criteria).offset(n).limit(n)`\n\nSupported primary domains:\n- **items**: Search for artifacts (files and folders)\n- **builds**: Search for build records\n- **entries**: Search for build artifact/dependency entries\n- **build.promotions**: Search for build promotions\n\nExample queries:\n- `items.find({\"repo\":\"libs-release-local\"})` - Find all items in a repo\n- `items.find({\"name\":{\"$match\":\"*.jar\"}})` - Find all JAR files\n- `items.find({\"type\":\"file\",\"size\":{\"$gt\":\"1000000\"}}).sort({\"$desc\":[\"size\"]}).limit(10)` - Top 10 largest files\n- `builds.find({\"name\":\"my-build\"}).include(\"module\")` - Find builds with modules",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "api",
                "search",
                "aql"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "description": "Your JFrog Platform deployment URL",
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "{{server}}",
                  "key": "server"
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "text/plain"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": null,
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "<string>"
            }
          },
